msgid "Release a new version"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Decide which number moves, raise only the part that changed, and let the"
" studies that use the package choose when to follow.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A version is a promise to the studies that declare it: **a version is "
"never reused**. The same id and version with another content is refused "
"by every tool and by every repository, so that a study never meets two "
"different packages under one name."
msgstr ""

msgid "Which number moves"
msgstr ""

msgid "Versions have three numbers, *major.minor.patch*:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**patch** (``0.1.0`` → ``0.1.1``) for labels, descriptions, colours and "
"styles;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**minor** (``0.1.0`` → ``0.2.0``) for new types, new concepts, new "
"points, new combiners, new commands;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**major** (``0.x`` → ``1.0.0``, ``1.x`` → ``2.0.0``) when a type is "
"removed or changes its meaning, its primitive or its operation."
msgstr ""

msgid "A package stays at ``0.x`` while it is ``proposed``."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each part has its own version"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An archive has its own ``version``; in a mixed package, ``[data]`` and "
"``[code]`` have theirs. **Raise only the part that changed**, and always "
"the archive:"
msgstr ""

msgid "What changed"
msgstr ""

msgid "``version``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[data].version`` and ``profile.json``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``[code].version``"
msgstr ""

msgid "a label of the data"
msgstr ""

msgid "0.2.0 → 0.2.1"
msgstr ""

msgid "0.1.0 → 0.1.1"
msgstr ""

msgid "unchanged"
msgstr ""

msgid "a fix in the code"
msgstr ""

msgid "a new command"
msgstr ""

msgid "0.2.0 → 0.3.0"
msgstr ""

msgid "0.1.0 → 0.2.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The data of a package keep their version in two places that must agree: "
"``[data].version`` in the envelope and ``version`` in ``profile.json`` "
"(for a package of data only, the archive's ``version`` is the data's). "
"The example studies of the package declare it in their header: raise it "
"there too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

msgid "Change the files, and the numbers as in the table."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"For a major version, write ``CHANGELOG.md`` beside the envelope: what "
"changes in meaning, and what a study should check. EMStudio shows it when"
" a study is about to follow a major version."
msgstr ""

msgid "Validate and build (see :doc:`test-and-validate`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Publish the archive beside the older ones (see :doc:`publish`). In em-"
"profiles, a pull request with the new version; the curators of the "
"package review it."
msgstr ""

msgid "What the people who use the package see"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**New data sit beside the old ones.** No study changes the version it "
"declares by itself: when a newer version is installed, the Extensions "
"window says that the open file uses an older one and offers **Update the "
"declaration to …**; for a major version, **What changes…** shows the "
"notes first, and **Keep the old one** leaves the file as it is."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**New code replaces the old one** on the computer, and the older versions"
" stay available under **Versions…**. EMStudio loads the new code at its "
"next start."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**The question of trust comes back only when the code asks for more**: "
"new permissions, new capabilities, or another origin. An update that "
"changes none of these installs with the trust already given."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**A review follows the code.** An update whose code section did not "
"change keeps its review; changed code is code nobody has read yet."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/extensions/install-packages-and-plugins`, *Use a package in"
" a study*."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
